# The Pages artifact. `dashboard/build.mjs` writes it and the `Dashboard` workflow rebuilds it on
# every publish, so a committed copy is stale the next time anything under `dashboard/` moves — and
# it would publish nothing anyway: that workflow's trigger is `paths: ['dashboard/**']`. Ignored so
# that building the page locally to look at it cannot end up in a commit.
site/
dashboard.html

# Blog drafts — published on WordPress, never from this repo
blog/

# One-off hand-run deploy scripts. `full_deploy.py` builds the datasets into ANOTHER workspace and
# leaves them there, so it hardcodes two real workspace GUIDs — and this repo is public, where every
# real GUID is a secret and no tracked file outside `history/` holds one. Ignored rather than
# sanitised: the reusable half is already in `fabric_run.py` (`REMOTE_LAKEHOUSE`), and what is left
# is a script whose whole value is naming the specific workspaces it points at.
full_deploy.py
